    "Reason : 1 - The Local Planning Authority are not satisfied that the use or operations described in the application would be lawful as the basement as built does not benefit from planning permission or nor has it been established that it is a lawful development. The proposed use for residential purposes in connection with the ground floor flat would result in a material amendment to the planning permission for the basement flat (refs.2020/1724 & 2020/3253) and would therefore constitute `development� as defined under Section 55 (1) of the Town & Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) for which planning permission would be required.",
